class.description:
[TimerInfo] describes a timer: countdown or stopwatch, length, looping, tick interval, alerts and clock. Assign it to [member Timer.timer_info] or pass it to [method TimerServer.create_timer]. It holds no running state; that lives in [TimerServer]. Changes to the resource apply live to the timers that use it.
The shown time is the time left for a countdown and the elapsed time for a stopwatch. [member alerts] and the time passed with [signal Timer.ticked] are in shown time.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var info = TimerInfo.new()
info.tick_mode = TimerInfo.TICK_MODE_STOPWATCH
info.tick_interval = 1.0
info.alerts = PackedFloat64Array([30.0, 60.0])
var timer = TimerServer.create_timer(info)
timer.start()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var info = new TimerInfo();
info.TickMode = TimerInfo.TimerTickMode.Stopwatch;
info.TickInterval = 1.0;
info.Alerts = new double[] { 30.0, 60.0 };
TimerInstance timer = TimerServer.CreateTimer(info);
timer.Start();
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
